Implemented `transpose.py:1` — replaces the `pass` stub with a working `transpose(text)`.

**Approach:** split on `\n`, pad each row on the right to the max width with a `\x00` sentinel, transpose column-by-column, then strip only *trailing sentinel* cells and map remaining sentinels to spaces. This preserves real input spaces (including intermittent padding like `1 3456`) while dropping end-of-row padding that has no source character.

